  {
    "name": "import_item",
    "description": "Preserve original text and create a searchable Markdown item. Set explicit=true only for a direct human request to re-add; this restores matching Trash records. Automatic jobs must use submit_sources/complete_intake and never set explicit. For interviews supply candidates=[canonical candidate names] to create/reuse candidate profiles under Interviews and link the session with an Interview tag; candidates are not authors. For a document use kind=document and projects=[project names]; it appears in Documents and every named project without copying. Supply doc_urls for Google Doc source identity and authors=[confirmed author names]. Supply document_people with verified owner, creator or mentioned roles and evidence; Google ownership must come from observed owner metadata. Omit date if unknown; documents display their Atlas added date. For a blog roundup use kind=blog, blog_feed=AI, and an edition date. Updates require start and exclusive end dates. For role=mentioned require observed email plus person_chip={personId,personProperties:{name,email}} from get_document, or person_link set to an explicit single-address mailto URL. Plain text names are not identity evidence; do not infer unknown names or emails.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "explicit": {
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "title": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "summary": {
          "type": "string"
        },
